WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.330
Honister Pass, Cumbria, December 2015.

2
00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:10.910
In 24 hours, Storm Desmond
dropped 341.4 millimetres of rain:

3
00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.690
a UK record.

4
00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:17.550
Other weeks bring cold, dry days,
with severe frost overnight.

5
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:22.690
In December 1952, fog
lay over London for days.

6
00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:23.650
Record rain.

7
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.130
Severe frost.

8
00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:26.690
Days of fog.

9
00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:27.990
Is it the mountains?

10
00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:30.690
What makes the weather here so changeable?

11
00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:34.090
In this mission, you'll learn
how highs and lows form,

12
00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:37.150
and read the clouds as a low passes over.

13
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:42.650
Then you'll find out how a fog over
London was trapped for days in 1952.

14
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:47.310
Your mission: explain why weather in
the British Isles is so changeable.
